     "body": "**Exploring a large codebase**:\n\n- **Scratchpad**: **write what you found** (file lists, dependencies, decisions) **to a file**, and refer to the file, not the conversation context. It survives the end of a session\n- **Subagents**: do the exploring (Explore) in a separate context and receive only a summary. The main context is preserved\n- **Manifest**: hold a progress list (done, not done, where results are) in a structured file → used for **resuming after a crash**. Do not rely on the model's memory for “how far did we get”\n- **`/compact`**: summarizes and shrinks the history. You can say what the summary should keep\n- Narrow with Glob → Grep → Read. Do not read every file. Read long files by line range\n\n### 🎓 Points to remember\n- Signs of degradation: answers stop being consistent. **It starts referring to “typical patterns” and not the specific classes it found earlier**\n- Responses: **a scratchpad file** (record key findings and refer to it from then on) / delegation to subagents (“find every test file”, “trace the dependencies of refund processing”) / a summary of each phase as the initial context of the next / `/compact` (say what to keep) / **crash recovery: each agent writes its state to a fixed location, and on resume the coordinator loads a manifest and puts it into each request**\n- Note: steering a long session means setting the scope in plan mode, saying what to keep when compacting, rewinding to correct course, and working in parallel with worktrees\n\n> “A migration of a large repository overflowed the context partway” → move progress out into a manifest, and hand files to subagents one at a time. “All of it in one session” is wrong.",
