     "body": "**Human review and confidence calibration**:\n\n- **Field-level confidence**: have a `confidence` output for each field of the extraction (0 to 1, or high/medium/low). One figure for the whole document buries the weak fields\n- **Calibration**: check against **a labeled validation set** that confidence matches the share that are right (are nine in ten of the items rated 0.9 correct?). If not, adjust the thresholds\n- **Stratified sampling**: draw the review sample by **document type, field and confidence band**. Random sampling alone misses the errors of the rarer types\n- **Accuracy by document type**: overall may be 97% while handwritten slips are at 70%. Measure by type, and set thresholds by type\n- Thresholds: low confidence, high value and new types go to a person. High confidence and low risk are automated\n\n### 🎓 Points to remember\n- **Overall accuracy hides weak segments** (97% overall, yet low for particular document types or fields). Before automating high-confidence extractions, check accuracy **by document type and by field**\n- **Stratified random sampling**: keep drawing from high-confidence extractions too, to measure the error rate (and catch new kinds of error) / have **confidence per field** output and calibrate the review threshold on a labeled validation set / routing to review: send people the extractions with low confidence and those whose source document is ambiguous or contradictory (concentrating limited time there)\n\n> “Overall accuracy is high, so drop human review” → wrong. “Stratify by type and confidence and send the low bands to people” is right.",
